   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3747"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phags pa byams pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byams pa mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreyanātha</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6118</idno><idno type="APIS">3747</idno><note type="comment">Future Buddha held as the author of the works that come to be designated as the "Five Jewels of Maitreya" (ID:6167).</note></person><person xml:id="person3756"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">asaṅga</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon thogs med</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">thogs myed</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6117</idno><idno type="APIS">3756</idno></person><person xml:id="person5963"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal gyi ming 'chang ba</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">དཔལ་གྱི་མིང་འཆང་བ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shAkya'i dge sbyong dpal gyi ming 'chang ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lho pa thugs rje dpal</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3CN19673</idno><idno type="APIS">5963</idno><note type="comment">Maybe the same person who authored a commentary on the Madhyāntavibhāga (ID:3748), two copies of which are listed in [GP444QCS]: 612: dpal gyi ming can (/dge slong dpal) gyis mdzad pa'i chos dang chos nyid rnam par 'bye dpa'i bstan bcos kyi rnam par bshad pa 'thad pa kun ldan&#13;
&#13;
Maybe the same person as Lho pa thugs rje dpal (bdr:P3CN19673).</note></person><person xml:id="person6033"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgyal sras chos dpal mgon po</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྒྱལ་སྲས་ཆོས་དཔལ་མགོན་པོ</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8LS13230</idno><idno type="APIS">6033</idno></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3749"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ratnagotravibhāga</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rātnagotravibhāga mahāyānottaratantraśāstra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">uttaratantra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po rgyud bla ma'i bstan bcos</title><author ref="person:3747">maitreya</author><author ref="person:3756">asaṅga</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The authorship of the work comes to be ascribed to the future Buddha Maitreya (ID:3747) in the Indian tradition from the 11th c. onward and in the Tibetan tradition. On earlier witnesses ascribing the authorship to Sāramati or Sthiramati, see [BAQ9MH4T]: 20-27. No attribution of that work to Asaṅga (ID:3756) was located in Indian sources, but the colophon of the Tibetan translation by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab ascribes the verses to Maitreya and the prose commentary to Asaṅga ([BAQ9MH4T]: 27-28).&#13;
There are six Tibetan translations, only that by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab and Sajjana is currently extant ([BAQ9MH4T]: chap. 6).</note><idno type="APIS">3749</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5474"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po mdo sde rgyan gyi rnam bshad 'thad pa kun ldan</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཐེག་པ་ཆེན་པོ་མདོ་སྡེ་རྒྱན་གྱི་རྣམ་བཤད་འཐད་པ་ཀུན་ལྡན</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po mdo sde rgyan gyi rnam bshad 'thad pa kun ldan</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1102-01-01">after 1102</date><author ref="person:5963">dpal gyi ming 'chang ba</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Date of composition: chu mo lug gi lo'i sa kha chen po'i zla ba = 1103, 1163, 1223, 1283, 1343, 1403</note><idno type="APIS">5474</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5478"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">theg pa chen po rgyud bla ma'i dka' gnad kyi mtha' dpyad mun sel</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཐེག་པ་ཆེན་པོ་རྒྱུད་བླ་མའི་དཀའ་གནད་ཀྱི་མཐའ་དཔྱད་མུན་སེལ</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><author ref="person:5963">dpal gyi ming 'chang ba</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Date of composition: stag gi* lo'i zla ba gr** pa'i dus</note><relatedItem type="commentaryOn" target="work:3749"/><idno type="APIS">5478</idno></bibl></listBibl><listPlace><place xml:id="place5733"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya dgon pa</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">ས་སྐྱ་དགོན་པ</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">dpal sa skyaʾi gtsug lag khang</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">dpal ldan sa skya'i gtsug lag chen po</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">dpal sa skya'i chos grwa chen po</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">dpal ldan sa skya'i chos grwa</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">sa skya dgon chen</placeName><location><geo>28.904203131982346 88.01762829101843</geo></location><idno type="APIS">5733